etc/uemacs.rc
    Added a ggr_opts flag to display control characters using the
    Unicode glyphs, rather than the 2-byte ^X.  If this is unset it
    reverts to the original ^X display, i.e.  the default with the
    standard start=up file is to use the Unicode glyphs.  This means
    that you will need your font to have the correct glyphs, or unset
    the bit.
    #define GGR_CTLGPH [estruct.h]
    Check the flag in vtputc() and act accordingly [display.c]
    Add a check for GGR_CTLGPH in the update_screenpos_for_char()
    define. [line.h]
    Change the test code to run twice, once with Ctlgph unset then again
    with it set.  Changed the column matching info accordingly.
    [autotest/search-with-nul.sh]
    Added a Ctlgph option to change-ggr-opts (and removed several
    unneeded delete-var lines). [etc/uemacs.rc]

